WEBVTT

1
00:00:50.151 --> 00:00:53.557
<i>Some people can see all your mistakes.</i>

2
00:00:54.557 --> 00:00:57.244
<i>The way you hold it in your shoulders.</i>

3
00:00:57.344 --> 00:00:59.910
<i>Show it in your face.</i>

4
00:01:01.664 --> 00:01:04.667
<i>I made a lot of mistakes in my life...</i>

5
00:01:05.330 --> 00:01:08.072
<i>and they were my mistakes.</i>

6
00:01:08.672 --> 00:01:10.802
<i>Nobody else's.</i>

7
00:01:11.241 --> 00:01:13.043
<i>Mine.</i>

8
00:01:13.703 --> 00:01:18.149
<i>When you get older, all those mistakes
start piling up inside you.</i>

9
00:01:19.349 --> 00:01:21.517
<i>Regrets...</i>

10
00:01:21.617 --> 00:01:23.470
<i>blame.</i>

11
00:01:24.020 --> 00:01:26.961
<i>It's enough to make you sick
to your stomach.</i>

12
00:01:29.425 --> 00:01:31.629
<i>Problem is...</i>

13
00:01:31.729 --> 00:01:35.781
<i>there are certain things
that I just can't change about myself.</i>

14
00:01:55.851 --> 00:01:58.019
Fill it up, will you?

15
00:02:04.460 --> 00:02:06.497
- Morning.
- Good morning.

16
00:02:06.597 --> 00:02:09.363
20 on eight, please?

17
00:02:12.935 --> 00:02:15.238
- Where are your cards?
- Cards...

18
00:02:15.338 --> 00:02:17.956
backside of this aisle right here.

19
00:02:31.337 --> 00:02:35.547
- He almost finished out there?
- Yeah, almost.

20
00:02:43.566 --> 00:02:46.313
<i>9-1-1. What's your emergency?</i>

21
00:02:46.937 --> 00:02:48.699
<i>Hello?</i>

22
00:02:48.799 --> 00:02:51.427
<i>What's the address of your emergency?</i>

23
00:02:54.777 --> 00:02:59.252
- That'll be it.
- Okay, 20 on the pump, $24.

24
00:02:59.352 --> 00:03:01.816
24. That's a steal.

25
00:03:07.423 --> 00:03:09.490
You have a good day.

26
00:03:16.665 --> 00:03:17.901
Boy.

27
00:03:25.658 --> 00:03:27.039
You're the one from the paper.

28
00:03:27.139 --> 00:03:31.448
I think you got me confused
with somebody else, all right?

29
00:03:31.548 --> 00:03:34.317
No. I know who you are.

30
00:03:34.417 --> 00:03:36.367
I know who he is too.

31
00:03:52.067 --> 00:03:55.751
The truth, sir...

32
00:05:00.502 --> 00:05:02.689
I assume you're a friend.

33
00:05:02.789 --> 00:05:06.443
- I'm sorry.
- A friend of the family?

34
00:05:06.543 --> 00:05:09.260
- Yeah.
- I'm sorry for your loss.

35
00:05:12.148 --> 00:05:16.720
- So what's gonna happen with the boy?
- He's going to his grandparents' place.

36
00:05:17.220 --> 00:05:20.912
- Where were they?
- They live in Farmington, New Mexico.

37
00:05:21.012 --> 00:05:24.516
But I hear his grandfather's
gravely ill.

38
00:05:24.616 --> 00:05:25.589
You driving him?

39
00:05:25.689 --> 00:05:29.016
No. I'm just gonna chauffeur him
over to the bus station.

40
00:05:29.116 --> 00:05:32.552
- Do you know Louis?
- No.

41
00:05:32.652 --> 00:05:36.054
- Thank the Lord, he's got his grandparents.
- Yeah.

42
00:05:38.824 --> 00:05:41.937
- All right, son. You ready?
- Yes, sir.

43
00:05:42.846 --> 00:05:45.113
Let me help you.

44
00:05:49.335 --> 00:05:51.402
Right over here.

45
00:06:00.796 --> 00:06:02.948
All right, son.

46
00:06:10.673 --> 00:06:13.544
So, all right. Here we go.

47
00:06:14.144 --> 00:06:16.377
Now I've got your ticket.
Your money's in the envelope.

48
00:06:16.477 --> 00:06:19.947
They're gonna put your skis
and bags underneath.

49
00:06:20.950 --> 00:06:23.153
I hate buses.

50
00:06:24.587 --> 00:06:27.369
- Can't you just drive me?
- No, son, I'm needed here.

51
00:06:27.469 --> 00:06:31.292
But you'll be fine.
Nothing to worry about, okay?

52
00:06:32.961 --> 00:06:35.515
It's... it was nice meeting you.

53
00:06:35.615 --> 00:06:37.948
You too, Louis.

54
00:06:40.018 --> 00:06:42.753
I'll be praying for you, son.

55
00:07:29.418 --> 00:07:31.945
Hey, Louis.

56
00:07:32.045 --> 00:07:35.158
- I'm John.
- Yeah, you were at the church.

57
00:07:35.258 --> 00:07:37.494
- That's right, that's right.
- Nice to meet you.

58
00:07:37.594 --> 00:07:40.728
Listen, I'm sorry about your mother.
It's a shame.

59
00:07:42.831 --> 00:07:45.202
Listen, I just got a phone call
from your grandparents.

60
00:07:45.302 --> 00:07:49.754
Apparently, they don't love the idea
of you riding on this bus for three days.

61
00:07:49.854 --> 00:07:51.657
They asked me if I'd give you a lift.

62
00:07:51.757 --> 00:07:55.442
Meanwhile, I was headed that way
so I told them, shit, why not?

63
00:07:57.280 --> 00:07:58.982
Sir, I don't know you.

64
00:07:59.082 --> 00:08:04.723
Yeah, I don't really know you either and,
frankly, this is a pain in my ass. But...

65
00:08:04.823 --> 00:08:07.840
like I said, I know your grandparents
and your mother was a...

66
00:08:07.940 --> 00:08:09.698
she was a good woman.

67
00:08:10.554 --> 00:08:12.087
You knew my mom?

68
00:08:13.363 --> 00:08:16.566
- Yeah.
- She never really talked about you.

69
00:08:16.666 --> 00:08:20.439
Yeah? Well, I guess I didn't make
much of an impression then, did I?

70
00:08:21.937 --> 00:08:24.030
We kept in touch. I'd call, she'd call.

71
00:08:24.130 --> 00:08:25.975
- Yeah. Yeah.
- You know how it goes.

72
00:08:26.075 --> 00:08:29.479
Listen, I got to hit the road. I understand
if you don't want to come with me.

73
00:08:29.579 --> 00:08:31.281
Besides, buses ain't so bad.

74
00:08:31.381 --> 00:08:35.752
Perfectly civilized mode
of transportation, if you ask me.

75
00:08:36.002 --> 00:08:38.238
But, hey...

76
00:08:38.988 --> 00:08:41.447
good luck to you, kid.

77
00:08:42.091 --> 00:08:46.526
And my deepest condolences
to you and your family, all right?

78
00:08:51.283 --> 00:08:54.025
Kid, you getting on the bus? I gotta go.

79
00:08:57.839 --> 00:09:00.908
Sir. Sir?

80
00:09:11.187 --> 00:09:13.075
Get in.

81
00:09:17.860 --> 00:09:21.965
You... you live in this car
or something?

82
00:09:22.365 --> 00:09:26.433
No, of course not.
I just wasn't expecting guests.

83
00:09:41.417 --> 00:09:44.218
Your mother was a wonderful woman.

84
00:09:44.318 --> 00:09:46.237
Classy lady.

85
00:09:46.337 --> 00:09:50.853
Fun gal. Full of spirit. She was...

86
00:09:52.053 --> 00:09:53.828
Sparky.

87
00:09:55.597 --> 00:09:58.565
- She was...
- I forgot.

88
00:09:59.468 --> 00:10:02.259
What do you got there? Pictures?

89
00:10:04.808 --> 00:10:09.748
- This is my grandparents' house.
- Oh, yeah, yeah. Good.

90
00:10:10.863 --> 00:10:12.744
That's good.

91
00:10:16.051 --> 00:10:19.756
You know, the only time I really
visited them was when I was little.

92
00:10:19.856 --> 00:10:22.825
Mom didn't get along
with my grandparents too well.

93
00:10:22.925 --> 00:10:25.359
Didn't really talk.

94
00:10:25.828 --> 00:10:29.697
- Hey, how long do you think it'll take?
- I don't know.

95
00:10:34.102 --> 00:10:35.897
What?

96
00:10:37.539 --> 00:10:39.406
Nothing.

97
00:10:41.126 --> 00:10:45.646
Hey, I got to make a couple quick calls.
Should just take me a couple minutes.

98
00:10:56.659 --> 00:10:59.962
- <i>Moody residence.</i>
- Mrs. Moody?

99
00:11:00.062 --> 00:11:02.699
John Wheeler here. How you doing?

100
00:11:02.799 --> 00:11:05.852
<i>You have got some nerve calling here.</i>

101
00:11:05.952 --> 00:11:08.772
I was just at your daughter's wake.
Where were you?

102
00:11:08.872 --> 00:11:10.824
<i>Earl's sick.</i>

103
00:11:10.924 --> 00:11:13.329
<i>Now what do you want?</i>

104
00:11:14.676 --> 00:11:18.815
- I got Louis, her boy.
- <i>What... why would you have Louis?</i>

105
00:11:18.915 --> 00:11:22.786
Now, look, there's been a change of plans.
I'm gonna drive him home.

106
00:11:22.886 --> 00:11:25.788
<i>Where's that priest?
Put Louis on the phone.</i>

107
00:11:25.888 --> 00:11:28.508
It'll just take a couple of days.
You got nothing to worry about.

108
00:11:28.608 --> 00:11:32.734
<i>Now you put Louis back
on that bus and get back...</i>

109
00:11:41.953 --> 00:11:44.187
One more stop.

110
00:12:14.570 --> 00:12:18.468
- Stay here.
- Hey, I need that to get home!

111
00:12:24.797 --> 00:12:27.023
What's up, John?

112
00:12:28.285 --> 00:12:32.095
Will you excuse us for a moment, please?
Okay, thanks.

113
00:12:50.873 --> 00:12:53.109
This is a fucking joke, right?

114
00:12:53.209 --> 00:12:55.645
There's a little over
6,000 bucks right there.

115
00:12:55.745 --> 00:12:59.382
You're short 14,000 and change.
Maybe more.

116
00:12:59.482 --> 00:13:03.436
Well, what are you... you said 10,000.
I owe you 10,000.

117
00:13:03.536 --> 00:13:06.770
You're late, John... again.

118
00:13:06.870 --> 00:13:08.775
So it's 20.

119
00:13:08.875 --> 00:13:10.951
What are you doing?

120
00:13:13.129 --> 00:13:17.467
- How long have we known each other?
- Long enough for you to know better.

121
00:13:17.567 --> 00:13:20.153
This is fucking bullshit, John!
Do you understand.

122
00:13:20.253 --> 00:13:21.768
What the fuck do you want from me?

123
00:13:24.200 --> 00:13:26.009
John...

124
00:13:26.109 --> 00:13:31.368
protection in jail is very expensive.
Do you understand that?

125
00:13:31.468 --> 00:13:34.350
I didn't ask you
for any goddamned protection.

126
00:13:34.450 --> 00:13:38.719
Yeah, but you took it. You know jail
could've been dangerous for you, John.

127
00:13:42.040 --> 00:13:44.508
I'm living out of my car.

128
00:13:46.594 --> 00:13:50.670
I don't have anything else. I just
gave you everything that I got, okay?

129
00:13:50.770 --> 00:13:53.036
Fine, do you want to go back to jail?

130
00:13:53.136 --> 00:13:55.905
You like the bed and the three meals
of crap they serve you every day?

131
00:13:56.005 --> 00:13:58.425
'Cause I can arrange that
with just one fucking phone call.

132
00:13:58.525 --> 00:14:02.479
- Freddy, give me the fucking phone.
- No, you're not gonna make any phone calls.

133
00:14:02.579 --> 00:14:05.781
I got just as much shit on you
as you got on me.

134
00:14:06.263 --> 00:14:09.115
6,000 bucks. That's all you get.

135
00:14:45.954 --> 00:14:48.070
We're closed!

136
00:14:48.790 --> 00:14:50.551
We're closed!

137
00:14:55.096 --> 00:14:57.231
Goddamn kid.

138
00:15:18.854 --> 00:15:20.921
Hey, are you in some kind of trouble?

139
00:15:24.176 --> 00:15:26.184
It's nothing.

140
00:15:29.131 --> 00:15:31.294
Did they do that to you?

141
00:15:31.701 --> 00:15:34.949
I don't know what I was thinking.
You ain't worth the trouble.

142
00:15:48.750 --> 00:15:51.322
The closest I could get you
is Albuquerque.

143
00:15:53.022 --> 00:15:56.731
I'll call your grandma and have her
pick you up in a couple of days.

144
00:15:57.293 --> 00:15:59.459
Good to meet you.

145
00:17:23.812 --> 00:17:25.679
Louis!

146
00:17:27.432 --> 00:17:29.033
Louis!

147
00:17:36.207 --> 00:17:37.974
Louis?

148
00:17:40.828 --> 00:17:42.558
Louis.

149
00:17:47.602 --> 00:17:49.341
Hey.

150
00:17:51.807 --> 00:17:54.033
Hey, I'm talking to you.

151
00:17:59.582 --> 00:18:02.179
I don't want to be alone.

152
00:18:09.290 --> 00:18:11.664
Why did she have to die?

153
00:18:14.929 --> 00:18:17.266
There's no good reason.

154
00:18:18.366 --> 00:18:20.600
I don't know, man.

155
00:18:21.303 --> 00:18:23.905
I don't have anyone else.

156
00:18:26.791 --> 00:18:30.205
Hey, you're gonna be all right.

157
00:19:28.103 --> 00:19:29.988
Hey!

158
00:19:31.308 --> 00:19:33.120
Hey!

159
00:19:35.076 --> 00:19:36.635
Hey, let's get something to eat.

160
00:19:38.213 --> 00:19:40.080
I'm hungry.

161
00:19:41.149 --> 00:19:43.485
What's with these skis?

162
00:19:43.893 --> 00:19:45.554
For skiing.

163
00:19:45.654 --> 00:19:48.181
Yeah, well, there ain't no snow
around here.

164
00:19:51.759 --> 00:19:55.531
- The skis were a gift from my mom.
- You probably never even skied before.

165
00:19:55.631 --> 00:19:58.334
- Yeah, she wanted me to learn.
- Skiing's expensive.

166
00:19:58.434 --> 00:20:00.229
I just saved you a shitload of money.

167
00:20:00.329 --> 00:20:02.304
It was the last thing
she gave me before she died.

168
00:20:02.404 --> 00:20:04.106
Yeah, it's a dumb sport.

169
00:20:04.206 --> 00:20:06.676
I can't believe all you got
was 20 bucks and that stupid ring!

170
00:20:06.776 --> 00:20:09.952
Are you hungry? I'm starving. Let's go.

171
00:20:19.355 --> 00:20:21.237
Good.

172
00:20:23.591 --> 00:20:25.965
What, you're not gonna eat?

173
00:20:26.528 --> 00:20:30.364
- I'm not hungry.
- Fine with me. Starve.

174
00:20:34.402 --> 00:20:36.936
Look at that little piece of ass.

175
00:20:39.707 --> 00:20:41.710
Hey, you like women?

176
00:20:41.810 --> 00:20:45.047
- Yeah, I guess.
- You guess?

177
00:20:45.347 --> 00:20:47.050
All right, well, know this...

178
00:20:47.150 --> 00:20:50.887
A scorned woman will tear your heart out,
put it between two buns and eat it

179
00:20:50.987 --> 00:20:53.504
just as your life slips away before you.

180
00:20:54.656 --> 00:20:57.023
Don't ever forget that.

181
00:20:57.692 --> 00:20:59.926
Hey, you wanna drive?

182
00:21:01.863 --> 00:21:03.998
Yeah? You wanna drive?

183
00:21:05.967 --> 00:21:08.103
All right, can you see over the hood?

184
00:21:08.203 --> 00:21:10.471
- I guess.
- All right.

185
00:21:10.571 --> 00:21:14.110
- Your feet touch the pedals?
- I think so.

186
00:21:14.210 --> 00:21:16.503
You think so or you can?
It's kind of a big deal.

187
00:21:16.603 --> 00:21:19.882
- Yeah, fine.
- Okay, all right. So this is an automatic.

188
00:21:19.982 --> 00:21:23.552
So all you gotta do is pull
that lever down from P to D.

189
00:21:23.652 --> 00:21:26.689
There you go. All right,
now take your foot off the brake.

190
00:21:26.789 --> 00:21:29.116
Push down on the gas.

191
00:21:30.292 --> 00:21:32.325
There you go.

192
00:21:36.397 --> 00:21:40.066
All you gotta do is avoid other cars
and that's pretty much it.

193
00:21:40.235 --> 00:21:41.981
How fast you going?

194
00:21:42.081 --> 00:21:44.744
- 32 mph.
- No, no, no. You gotta get it up.

195
00:21:44.844 --> 00:21:47.641
At least 50 or 60, even 70.

196
00:21:50.295 --> 00:21:51.866
There you go.

197
00:21:52.532 --> 00:21:54.412
See, faster is way better, isn't it?

198
00:21:56.752 --> 00:21:58.789
You're blind!

199
00:22:03.624 --> 00:22:07.596
All right, the first rule
to gun fighting is having a gun.

200
00:22:07.696 --> 00:22:11.644
All right, I prefer to have something small.
Something easier to carry.

201
00:22:11.744 --> 00:22:16.288
Easier to conceal, all right? You can't go
hunting with something like this, though.

202
00:22:16.388 --> 00:22:20.242
- Why not?
- You just can't. It ain't right.

203
00:22:20.342 --> 00:22:24.728
- What's the point, then?
- The point is, if I have the gun...

204
00:22:25.748 --> 00:22:29.301
I have the control, right?

205
00:22:29.520 --> 00:22:31.884
You want to give it a shot?

206
00:22:34.422 --> 00:22:36.759
If I let you shoot this,
you owe me a favor.

207
00:22:36.859 --> 00:22:39.699
- Okay.
- All right.

208
00:22:42.330 --> 00:22:44.337
Go ahead.

209
00:22:52.458 --> 00:22:55.085
Go ahead, shoot it again.

210
00:22:58.638 --> 00:23:01.719
All right. Turn it, gangster style.

211
00:23:03.299 --> 00:23:04.868
There you go.

212
00:23:06.955 --> 00:23:08.788
Let's go.

213
00:23:13.127 --> 00:23:15.295
Hey, give me my gun.

214
00:23:34.749 --> 00:23:38.254
Wake up. Wake up.

215
00:23:40.205 --> 00:23:42.639
It's time for that favor.

216
00:24:02.543 --> 00:24:05.314
All right, now keep the engine running.

217
00:24:05.414 --> 00:24:07.780
Don't turn it off for any reason,
you understand?

218
00:24:07.880 --> 00:24:09.077
Where you going?

219
00:24:09.177 --> 00:24:12.021
I gotta run inside
and grab a couple of things.

220
00:24:12.121 --> 00:24:15.591
Just keep it running. I'll be right back.
Now jump in the driver's seat.

221
00:24:15.691 --> 00:24:17.596
Wait, what?

222
00:24:31.338 --> 00:24:33.873
- Howdy.
- Howdy.

223
00:24:37.662 --> 00:24:41.083
Let me know if I can help you
with anything.

224
00:24:41.183 --> 00:24:44.651
We got some specials back there.

225
00:25:24.225 --> 00:25:25.963
Are you gonna get it?

226
00:25:26.063 --> 00:25:28.692
Yeah, that should... oh, the newspaper.

227
00:25:30.399 --> 00:25:31.632
Get on the ground.

228
00:25:37.305 --> 00:25:38.783
Get on the fucking ground!

229
00:25:40.892 --> 00:25:43.787
Get on the goddamn...
I'll beat you with this fucking gun!

230
00:25:43.887 --> 00:25:45.954
I heard you, damn it!

231
00:26:04.231 --> 00:26:07.869
Listen, this store's all I got.
You leave me something, you hear?

232
00:26:07.969 --> 00:26:11.404
- There you go.
- You're a real son of a bitch.

233
00:26:15.276 --> 00:26:19.115
Hey! What the hell are you doing?
Hey, hey!

234
00:26:19.915 --> 00:26:21.550
Get out of the fucking car! Get out...

235
00:26:21.650 --> 00:26:25.187
- Hands off the boy!
- Hey, easy, easy!

236
00:26:25.687 --> 00:26:27.354
Go!

237
00:26:33.762 --> 00:26:37.297
All right. Now keep it up over 70.
Keep it on the right side of the road.

238
00:26:37.397 --> 00:26:39.239
- Just like I told you.
- I'm gonna be sick.

239
00:26:39.339 --> 00:26:41.608
- What do you mean, you feel sick?
- I'm sick, I'm sick.

240
00:26:41.708 --> 00:26:43.973
What are you doing? Hey! Hey!

241
00:26:44.073 --> 00:26:48.375
Get in the back! Get in the back!
Go, go, go, go, go!

242
00:26:52.913 --> 00:26:56.316
Oh, shit! God damn it!

243
00:26:59.920 --> 00:27:01.623
Son of a bitch!

244
00:27:01.723 --> 00:27:04.057
- I need some air.
- Yeah, well, shut up!

245
00:27:07.628 --> 00:27:09.664
I need air.

246
00:27:13.351 --> 00:27:16.360
- I need some air.
- What are you doing? Shut that door!

247
00:27:20.058 --> 00:27:21.175
No!

248
00:27:27.147 --> 00:27:30.764
No! God damn it!

249
00:27:30.864 --> 00:27:32.969
God damn it!

250
00:27:47.101 --> 00:27:49.163
Stay here.

251
00:27:49.713 --> 00:27:51.654
Where you going?

252
00:28:09.657 --> 00:28:11.737
Get your things.

253
00:28:12.193 --> 00:28:14.529
- Where'd you get that car?
- Shut up and get in!

254
00:28:14.629 --> 00:28:15.698
Did you steal it?

255
00:28:15.798 --> 00:28:18.971
I will leave you here.
I swear to God, I will!

256
00:28:39.837 --> 00:28:42.228
You cost me a lot of money today.

257
00:28:42.958 --> 00:28:45.573
I don't want anything to do with you.

258
00:28:46.544 --> 00:28:49.348
Well, that's not an option, is it?

259
00:28:50.048 --> 00:28:52.639
You can't make me stay.

260
00:28:52.968 --> 00:28:56.304
I can leave. Just hitchhike.

261
00:28:56.404 --> 00:29:00.940
- Yeah, okay. You're gonna hitchhike?
- Yeah.

262
00:29:06.347 --> 00:29:09.445
Why don't we find a place
to sleep tonight?

263
00:29:10.119 --> 00:29:13.865
- With a bed?
- Yeah, sure. Why not?

264
00:29:15.323 --> 00:29:17.190
Fine.

265
00:29:27.835 --> 00:29:29.928
You awake?

266
00:29:30.438 --> 00:29:34.007
- What?
- Just wanted to see if you were awake.

267
00:29:39.647 --> 00:29:42.859
- Why'd you do it?
- Do what?

268
00:29:42.959 --> 00:29:44.986
Rob that place.

269
00:29:45.086 --> 00:29:48.524
Because we didn't have any money
and we needed it.

270
00:29:49.424 --> 00:29:52.661
- To get me home?
- Yeah, to get you home.

271
00:29:52.761 --> 00:29:56.429
Food and gas. This bed.

272
00:29:57.966 --> 00:30:00.304
Why do you live in your car?

273
00:30:02.669 --> 00:30:05.340
Because I can't afford anything else.

274
00:30:05.440 --> 00:30:07.806
- Most adults have jobs...
- Just go to bed, Louis.

275
00:30:07.906 --> 00:30:11.611
Just go the fuck to bed, please.

276
00:31:16.560 --> 00:31:18.727
All right.

277
00:31:20.347 --> 00:31:24.086
When you're done in there, I want you
to pull the truck around. Understand?

278
00:31:24.186 --> 00:31:28.725
- Hey, you paying attention to me?
- Yeah.

279
00:31:28.825 --> 00:31:32.060
- I heard you.
- God damn it, you pay attention!

280
00:31:32.160 --> 00:31:36.845
Wake up! You're not gonna
go fucking this up for me again.

281
00:32:05.759 --> 00:32:08.630
All right, Louis. Stop fucking around
and open up the door.

282
00:32:08.730 --> 00:32:10.798
A couple of days.

283
00:32:10.898 --> 00:32:13.603
That's how long you said it would take.
You're a liar.

284
00:32:14.803 --> 00:32:17.073
Open up the door.

285
00:32:18.473 --> 00:32:20.272
Come on!

286
00:32:21.075 --> 00:32:24.179
Fucking... Open up the fucking door!

287
00:32:24.279 --> 00:32:26.064
God damn it! Okay.

288
00:32:26.164 --> 00:32:29.885
Now take your hands off the wheel
and get out of the car.

289
00:32:29.985 --> 00:32:32.940
Just one more day and I'll take you
to your grandparent's? Now come on.

290
00:32:33.040 --> 00:32:34.981
Open it up.

291
00:32:35.381 --> 00:32:37.274
Please.

292
00:32:40.911 --> 00:32:42.886
You need me.

293
00:32:54.519 --> 00:32:57.629
Hello. How's your day?

294
00:32:57.729 --> 00:33:00.782
Oh, just... going great.

295
00:33:00.882 --> 00:33:05.327
- Good-looking boy you got there.
- Yeah, yeah, he is adorable, isn't he?

296
00:33:05.427 --> 00:33:07.088
Got a daughter myself.

297
00:33:08.279 --> 00:33:11.071
- I'll take 20 on two, please.
- No gas.

298
00:33:11.271 --> 00:33:15.554
- Pump's broke. Been broke for months.
- Oh, shit, all right.

299
00:33:16.130 --> 00:33:20.066
Would you grab me a can
of that Black Bear Longcut Wintergreen?

300
00:33:24.822 --> 00:33:27.490
You don't want any trouble now, do you?

301
00:33:30.577 --> 00:33:33.515
- Open it up.
- Yeah. Ain't much in there.

302
00:33:33.615 --> 00:33:35.781
Well, that'll do.

303
00:33:38.602 --> 00:33:41.678
Boy, what are you doing? Come on!
This ain't no fucking library! Hurry up!

304
00:33:41.778 --> 00:33:45.759
Quit pissing around! Now get back there
and clean that up. Come on.

305
00:34:01.258 --> 00:34:03.156
Come on.

306
00:34:04.279 --> 00:34:07.382
In and out just like a couple of ghosts.

307
00:34:07.482 --> 00:34:09.281
Gimme that.

308
00:34:12.653 --> 00:34:14.487
Thank you, sir.

309
00:34:23.864 --> 00:34:26.299
You got a safe?

310
00:34:42.250 --> 00:34:43.771
Christ!

311
00:34:44.486 --> 00:34:46.752
Go, go, go, go!

312
00:34:53.361 --> 00:34:55.976
Fuck you!

313
00:34:58.233 --> 00:34:59.578
God damn it!

314
00:35:00.937 --> 00:35:04.465
God damn it, I can't believe that.

315
00:35:04.565 --> 00:35:06.406
Shit.

316
00:35:07.542 --> 00:35:12.487
I'll tell you what, boy. Life can be
such a bore sometimes. But this...

317
00:35:12.587 --> 00:35:15.984
this... this is great.

318
00:35:16.584 --> 00:35:19.387
Well, don't look at me like that.

319
00:35:19.487 --> 00:35:23.508
You and me make
a really, really good team.

320
00:35:23.608 --> 00:35:27.078
Shit, they probably got nicknames
for us already.

321
00:35:27.178 --> 00:35:30.532
- Who? The papers?
- Yeah.

322
00:35:31.322 --> 00:35:33.285
- Don't they have better things to do?
- Shit, no.

323
00:35:33.385 --> 00:35:35.597
Bonnie and Clyde
was all over the newspapers.

324
00:35:35.697 --> 00:35:38.354
Billy the Kid, too. He was famous.

325
00:35:38.454 --> 00:35:41.977
- Like in movies?
- Exactly.

326
00:35:42.677 --> 00:35:46.482
You know, in the movies,
they... they all got shot...

327
00:35:46.882 --> 00:35:48.769
to death.

328
00:35:50.784 --> 00:35:52.587
Aren't you having fun?

329
00:35:52.687 --> 00:35:56.789
- If I was your age, I'd be having fun.
- No, I'm not having fun.

330
00:36:00.594 --> 00:36:04.178
You think this is easy for me? Dragging
your skinny little ass all over the place?

331
00:36:04.278 --> 00:36:07.034
This ain't no fucking holiday,
all right?

332
00:36:07.134 --> 00:36:10.236
This is a job.
This is work driving you home.

333
00:36:15.208 --> 00:36:18.296
You know, it'll all be over
soon enough, all right?

334
00:36:18.396 --> 00:36:20.637
Yeah, I hope so.

335
00:36:23.183 --> 00:36:25.372
Did you...

336
00:36:26.754 --> 00:36:30.191
Did you see that shotgun
under the counter earlier today?

337
00:36:30.291 --> 00:36:32.727
- No.
- No?

338
00:36:32.827 --> 00:36:35.487
I just figured you might've seen it
underneath there when you were,

339
00:36:35.587 --> 00:36:38.448
- you know, down below...
- I didn't see any gun.

340
00:36:40.300 --> 00:36:42.105
Okay.

341
00:36:47.507 --> 00:36:51.498
Ma'am? Do you have chocolate ice cream?

342
00:36:52.097 --> 00:36:54.282
I'll have to check in the freezer.

343
00:36:54.382 --> 00:36:57.219
Okay. Well, we'd like one scoop.

344
00:36:57.319 --> 00:36:59.920
Two spoons for me and the boy, please.

345
00:37:00.020 --> 00:37:02.783
- One scoop and two spoons.
- Two spoons. That's right.

346
00:37:02.883 --> 00:37:04.856
Okay.

347
00:37:09.580 --> 00:37:10.848
Let's go.

348
00:37:12.040 --> 00:37:14.369
- Ice cream.
- We're leaving. Come on.

349
00:37:14.469 --> 00:37:17.355
- We have plenty of money.
- We gotta keep moving.

350
00:37:17.455 --> 00:37:20.990
- I'm not even done eating yet.
- Yes, you are. Let's go.

351
00:37:32.185 --> 00:37:34.184
Get out here!

352
00:37:35.756 --> 00:37:38.130
- God damn it.
- There you go, honey.

353
00:37:38.230 --> 00:37:41.396
One scoop and two spoons.

354
00:37:41.496 --> 00:37:44.065
- I love chocolate.
- Thank you.

355
00:37:44.965 --> 00:37:47.626
Oh, he just needed some fresh air.

356
00:37:47.726 --> 00:37:49.278
- He'll be back, right?
- Yes.

357
00:37:49.378 --> 00:37:50.921
Okay.

358
00:37:51.021 --> 00:37:53.544
I can... I can share if you want some.

359
00:37:53.644 --> 00:37:57.913
Honey, I don't need the calories.
You enjoy that chocolate ice cream.

360
00:37:58.013 --> 00:38:00.615
Let me know if I can do
something for you.

361
00:38:00.715 --> 00:38:02.448
Thank you.

362
00:38:15.863 --> 00:38:18.366
That'll be 14.50.

363
00:38:18.466 --> 00:38:21.590
- Thank you.
- You're welcome, sweetie.

364
00:38:24.338 --> 00:38:29.844
I'll tell you what. You tell his mama
that she raised a gem of a boy.

365
00:38:29.944 --> 00:38:32.578
Yeah, I'll be sure to tell her that.

366
00:39:25.599 --> 00:39:28.219
We gotta get rid of that truck.

367
00:39:28.319 --> 00:39:30.120
I like that truck.

368
00:39:30.220 --> 00:39:33.072
Yeah, well,
it's not safe to drive anymore.

369
00:40:05.239 --> 00:40:08.291
Come on, let's go.

370
00:40:14.481 --> 00:40:19.357
Hey, hey, hey, hey!
Come on, lady! I got a kid here!

371
00:40:21.155 --> 00:40:23.458
- Jesus Christ.
- We should have kept the truck.

372
00:40:23.558 --> 00:40:25.621
Yeah, well...

373
00:40:26.144 --> 00:40:28.030
Hey!

374
00:40:29.930 --> 00:40:31.713
Just keep walking.

375
00:40:31.813 --> 00:40:34.043
Just keep walking.

376
00:40:37.438 --> 00:40:40.008
Shit! Keep your mouth shut.

377
00:40:40.108 --> 00:40:43.075
Neither one of us
want to go to jail, right?

378
00:40:49.716 --> 00:40:51.850
Hello, Officer!

379
00:40:52.619 --> 00:40:57.191
Hitchhiking is illegal.
Particularly on Sunday.

380
00:40:57.491 --> 00:41:00.127
Yeah, our car broke down.

381
00:41:01.415 --> 00:41:04.663
Let me see some ID. Come on.

382
00:41:08.101 --> 00:41:11.439
Turn around, over there.
Spread your legs. Come on.

383
00:41:11.539 --> 00:41:13.407
Where you headed?

384
00:41:14.206 --> 00:41:16.577
His grandparents' place.

385
00:41:17.161 --> 00:41:18.613
I'm real sorry about this, Officer.

386
00:41:18.713 --> 00:41:21.546
It's just that, you know,
we didn't have much of a choice.

387
00:41:21.646 --> 00:41:25.052
Our truck broke down back there, so...

388
00:41:25.152 --> 00:41:28.686
Well, now is it a car or is it a truck?

389
00:41:30.490 --> 00:41:32.960
He meant... he meant car.

390
00:41:33.060 --> 00:41:36.697
You better both come with me.
We'll clear this up down at the station.

391
00:41:36.797 --> 00:41:38.538
Come on.

392
00:41:46.239 --> 00:41:47.642
Sir?

393
00:41:48.242 --> 00:41:51.829
- We're just... we're on our way to church.
- What was that?

394
00:41:51.929 --> 00:41:55.266
We're going to church
to pray for my mom.

395
00:41:55.366 --> 00:41:57.652
Yeah, his mama died.

396
00:41:57.752 --> 00:41:59.787
- Is that right?
- Yeah.

397
00:41:59.887 --> 00:42:05.059
- Is that right, son? Your mama just died?
- Yes, sir. Just last week.

398
00:42:05.159 --> 00:42:07.162
I'm sorry to hear that.

399
00:42:07.262 --> 00:42:09.590
All right, get in the car.
I'll give you a ride. Come on.

400
00:42:09.690 --> 00:42:12.200
- No, no, we can do...
- No, it's all right. Don't worry.

401
00:42:12.600 --> 00:42:14.740
Come on. Don't make me wait.

402
00:42:15.970 --> 00:42:18.399
Can I... can I sit in the front?

403
00:42:18.499 --> 00:42:20.239
Sure.

404
00:42:25.078 --> 00:42:27.346
Thank you, Officer!

405
00:42:30.450 --> 00:42:33.321
All right, let's get
the hell out of here.

406
00:42:34.521 --> 00:42:37.558
Hey, where you going?

407
00:42:37.658 --> 00:42:39.243
Church.

408
00:42:39.343 --> 00:42:41.221
Louis?

409
00:43:21.768 --> 00:43:24.205
- Praise the Lord!
- Praise the Lord!

410
00:43:24.505 --> 00:43:26.741
- Amen!
- Amen!

411
00:43:26.841 --> 00:43:30.743
I am so pleased to see
some visitors with us this morning.

412
00:43:32.195 --> 00:43:34.532
Come on up here, son.

413
00:43:35.182 --> 00:43:39.103
Come on up here, son!
I'm not gonna bite you.

414
00:43:39.203 --> 00:43:43.290
Come join me here.
There you go. Let him by there.

415
00:43:43.390 --> 00:43:45.126
Here you are.

416
00:43:45.226 --> 00:43:47.528
What is your name, son?

417
00:43:47.628 --> 00:43:48.976
- Louis.
- Louis.

418
00:43:49.076 --> 00:43:51.933
Everyone please welcome
our child of God, Louis.

419
00:43:52.033 --> 00:43:54.201
Welcome, Louis.

420
00:43:54.301 --> 00:43:56.359
What is your name?

421
00:43:56.459 --> 00:43:57.890
- John.
- John?

422
00:43:57.990 --> 00:43:59.674
- Yep.
- Why won't you join us?

423
00:43:59.774 --> 00:44:01.176
Nah, I'm good right here.

424
00:44:01.276 --> 00:44:03.584
No, no. I'm extending my hand
in the name of the Lord

425
00:44:03.684 --> 00:44:06.143
so we may greet you as a congregation.

426
00:44:06.243 --> 00:44:09.881
If you wouldn't mind removing your cap
here in the house of the Lord?

427
00:44:13.820 --> 00:44:19.460
Everyone please welcome
these brothers in Christ, John and Louis.

428
00:44:19.560 --> 00:44:21.829
Welcome, John and Louis.

429
00:44:21.929 --> 00:44:23.817
Thank you.

430
00:44:24.765 --> 00:44:27.568
- Thank you.
- Yeah, yeah. Can we sit?

431
00:44:27.668 --> 00:44:30.622
- Please do. Take your seat, gentlemen.
- All right.

432
00:44:46.452 --> 00:44:50.666
We don't see too many new faces
around here. It's exciting when we do.

433
00:44:51.058 --> 00:44:53.027
We won't be staying for long.

434
00:44:53.127 --> 00:44:56.164
- What, you just passing through?
- Yeah.

435
00:44:56.764 --> 00:45:00.234
Listen, I want you to know something.
You're welcome to stay as long as you like.

436
00:45:00.334 --> 00:45:03.721
My mission is to grow this family.

437
00:45:03.821 --> 00:45:06.230
Spread the word of God.

438
00:45:06.774 --> 00:45:08.993
Well, like I said...

439
00:45:09.596 --> 00:45:11.034
we won't be staying for long.

440
00:45:12.745 --> 00:45:14.546
All right.

441
00:45:15.915 --> 00:45:18.152
He's a quiet one.

442
00:45:18.252 --> 00:45:21.823
- Got many friends?
- I have no idea.

443
00:45:21.923 --> 00:45:26.026
A boy needs friends, you know.
Jesus had 12 of them.

444
00:45:26.126 --> 00:45:29.460
Yeah. Well, look what good that did him.

445
00:45:30.163 --> 00:45:33.567
Listen, we're having a retreat tonight.
Want to stick around? The boy will love it.

446
00:45:33.667 --> 00:45:35.787
You gonna have food there?

447
00:45:36.603 --> 00:45:39.373
We'll have food there. Yeah.

448
00:45:40.073 --> 00:45:43.444
- One piece of advice.
- What's that?

449
00:45:43.844 --> 00:45:46.881
You want to save a little room
for the coconut cream pie.

450
00:45:47.431 --> 00:45:49.297
Good to know.

451
00:45:50.416 --> 00:45:52.592
- Louis, hello, my friend.
- Hi.

452
00:45:52.692 --> 00:45:54.393
- How are you, son?
- Good, thank you.

453
00:45:54.493 --> 00:45:56.490
I'm gonna sit here
and join you if you don't mind.

454
00:45:56.590 --> 00:45:58.659
- It's fine.
- We're happy to have you with us.

455
00:45:58.759 --> 00:46:00.894
Happy to be here.

456
00:46:00.994 --> 00:46:03.295
So tell me about yourself.

457
00:46:39.532 --> 00:46:40.902
Hey.

458
00:46:41.002 --> 00:46:44.099
Louis. Louis? Hey, hey, hey, wake up.

459
00:46:48.108 --> 00:46:51.310
- We gotta hit the road. Come on.
- What the hell is...

460
00:46:56.015 --> 00:46:59.919
What the hell are you doing?
I don't want... I'm not fucking leaving!

461
00:47:00.019 --> 00:47:02.582
- Come on, it's time to go.
- What the hell's your problem?

462
00:47:02.682 --> 00:47:04.690
Hey, come on!

463
00:47:06.826 --> 00:47:08.660
Come on!

464
00:47:15.368 --> 00:47:17.369
Here's yours.

465
00:47:27.146 --> 00:47:29.214
I hate you.

466
00:47:30.216 --> 00:47:32.152
I think you were scared.

467
00:47:32.252 --> 00:47:35.456
You're scared they'd find out
you're a bad person.

468
00:47:35.556 --> 00:47:38.359
A wolf, like the pastor said.

469
00:47:38.459 --> 00:47:41.528
A wolf? He called me a wolf?

470
00:47:41.628 --> 00:47:44.298
Beware of false prophets
who wear sheep's clothing

471
00:47:44.398 --> 00:47:47.618
because really they're ravenous wolves.

472
00:47:48.969 --> 00:47:50.989
He said that?

473
00:47:52.372 --> 00:47:54.726
That's...

474
00:47:55.209 --> 00:47:56.412
I'm not doing this anymore.

475
00:47:56.512 --> 00:47:58.880
- What do you mean, you're not doing it?
- I'm not doing it.

476
00:47:58.980 --> 00:48:03.064
Come... hey, get up! Come on!
We've been over this!

477
00:48:03.684 --> 00:48:05.653
Hey, get up!

478
00:48:05.753 --> 00:48:07.752
We gotta keep moving.

479
00:48:09.939 --> 00:48:11.372
Hey!

480
00:48:11.472 --> 00:48:15.093
Can't just sit around all day!
Come on! Let's go!

481
00:48:26.939 --> 00:48:28.809
Thank you.

482
00:48:28.909 --> 00:48:32.324
I need a lift for me and my friend back here.
Just take a minute. Hold on one second.

483
00:48:32.424 --> 00:48:34.830
Louis! Come on!

484
00:48:44.857 --> 00:48:47.058
Louis.

485
00:49:06.579 --> 00:49:09.950
Grab our things and take them to the room,
will ya? I'm gonna go grab a drink.

486
00:49:10.050 --> 00:49:13.952
- How long?
- I don't know. As long as it takes me.

487
00:49:23.296 --> 00:49:26.331
Give me a whiskey and a beer chaser.

488
00:49:58.398 --> 00:50:00.317
Oh, God.

489
00:50:00.417 --> 00:50:02.187
Okay.

490
00:51:18.511 --> 00:51:19.947
I don't know where the damn kid is.

491
00:51:20.047 --> 00:51:22.616
How can you drink those things?
They give me heartburn.

492
00:51:22.716 --> 00:51:26.585
Yeah? I think they're just fine
in the morning.

493
00:51:28.921 --> 00:51:32.246
- Oh, there he is!
- Great.

494
00:51:32.346 --> 00:51:34.074
This is Louis,

495
00:51:34.174 --> 00:51:36.522
- Louis Moody.
- Hi.

496
00:51:36.622 --> 00:51:40.702
Hi, honey. I'm Mary. This is Rose.

497
00:51:41.802 --> 00:51:45.506
- Mary and Rose are headed into Mexico.
- That's right. You're gonna pay for the gas.

498
00:51:45.606 --> 00:51:49.450
- 'Cause she pissed off our meal ticket!
- Oh, Rose, shut up!

499
00:51:49.910 --> 00:51:51.445
So there you have it.

500
00:51:51.545 --> 00:51:54.712
- Well, get in. You're driving, right?
- Oh, yeah.

501
00:51:58.448 --> 00:51:59.896
Should I put the stuff in the trunk?

502
00:51:59.996 --> 00:52:02.929
- Just throw it in the back.
- Back there?

503
00:52:03.029 --> 00:52:04.892
Why don't you guys both
get in the way back?

504
00:52:04.992 --> 00:52:08.994
We got some adult conversations to have.

505
00:52:13.399 --> 00:52:15.634
- Get in.
- This is gonna be fun.

506
00:52:29.949 --> 00:52:32.601
Were you the one knocking on my wall?

507
00:52:33.486 --> 00:52:35.122
No.

508
00:52:35.222 --> 00:52:37.710
Yes, you were.

509
00:52:38.325 --> 00:52:40.126
Why didn't you knock back?

510
00:52:40.226 --> 00:52:43.096
That's how it works, you know.
You're supposed to knock back.

511
00:52:43.196 --> 00:52:44.798
I don't know.

512
00:52:45.398 --> 00:52:48.569
- How old are you anyway?
- I'm 13.

513
00:52:48.669 --> 00:52:51.838
Well, I mean, I guess, 14.

514
00:52:52.138 --> 00:52:54.039
I'm 13.

515
00:52:55.275 --> 00:52:57.820
Is that... is that your mom?

516
00:52:57.920 --> 00:52:59.553
You could call her that.

517
00:52:59.653 --> 00:53:02.498
It's just that you don't look
like each other...

518
00:53:02.838 --> 00:53:04.885
so... I was just wondering.

519
00:53:04.985 --> 00:53:06.978
People say I take after my dad.

520
00:53:08.389 --> 00:53:11.112
People say I take after my mom.

521
00:53:20.332 --> 00:53:22.692
That's an amethyst.

522
00:53:23.937 --> 00:53:25.655
- That's turquoise.
- I know turquoise.

523
00:53:25.755 --> 00:53:30.210
I got a... check that out.
Brand new ring.

524
00:53:30.310 --> 00:53:32.913
- That's nice.
- See that? Turquoise.

525
00:53:33.013 --> 00:53:36.217
- Well, that's what they call kismet.
- Oh, yeah? What's that mean?

526
00:53:36.317 --> 00:53:40.994
Well, it's a Middle Eastern word
for coincidence or serendipity.

527
00:53:41.472 --> 00:53:43.190
Kismet.

528
00:53:43.590 --> 00:53:45.813
- Kismet.
- So here's the deal.

529
00:53:45.913 --> 00:53:48.895
You pay for the gas.
We'll pay for our own lodging, okay?

530
00:53:48.995 --> 00:53:50.390
All right.

531
00:53:50.490 --> 00:53:53.533
You know, I don't just let
any stranger into my car.

532
00:53:53.633 --> 00:53:55.569
These are unique circumstances,
you understand?

533
00:53:55.669 --> 00:53:57.986
I understand completely.

534
00:53:58.372 --> 00:54:01.408
And we're not exactly strangers
at this point.

535
00:54:01.508 --> 00:54:04.111
Just don't get any ideas, lover boy.

536
00:54:04.211 --> 00:54:08.049
I won't get any.
Well, I might get a couple ideas.

537
00:54:09.099 --> 00:54:11.666
I'll just keep 'em right up in here.

538
00:54:37.843 --> 00:54:41.669
Don't go telling 'em too much about yourself.
Remember what I told you about women.

539
00:54:43.383 --> 00:54:46.053
Well, look at us.
Just like one big happy family.

540
00:54:46.153 --> 00:54:47.956
Hardly.

541
00:54:48.418 --> 00:54:50.991
Hey, you know what I think we should do?
We should go shopping.

542
00:54:51.291 --> 00:54:53.860
Might as well have a little fun
while we're on this trip, right?

543
00:54:53.960 --> 00:54:55.913
I don't know.

544
00:54:56.013 --> 00:54:58.412
She loves buying stuff.

545
00:55:00.533 --> 00:55:02.591
All right, y'all.

546
00:55:02.991 --> 00:55:04.343
What do you think?

547
00:55:05.008 --> 00:55:07.989
Well, well, well.
Just like Miss America.

548
00:55:08.642 --> 00:55:12.012
- So can we go now?
- I'm gonna buy that for you.

549
00:55:12.112 --> 00:55:15.165
- We need that money.
- I got plenty.

550
00:55:15.265 --> 00:55:17.693
I'm gonna go pick out
some things for the kids.

551
00:55:26.392 --> 00:55:28.889
Oh, yeah.

552
00:55:31.248 --> 00:55:34.238
- I hate dresses.
- You two look adorable.

553
00:55:35.318 --> 00:55:37.385
You look nice.

554
00:55:54.053 --> 00:55:58.341
You know, I'm usually a pretty good judge
of character. But I'm gonna admit...

555
00:55:58.441 --> 00:56:01.639
I read y'all wrong.
I thought you were gonna be...

556
00:56:02.139 --> 00:56:05.799
greedy and selfish like most
of the men I've been with.

557
00:56:06.049 --> 00:56:08.215
But you ain't...

558
00:56:08.772 --> 00:56:10.551
and I like you.

559
00:56:10.651 --> 00:56:13.206
Yeah? Well, I like you too.

560
00:56:16.492 --> 00:56:19.029
You know, my mama always said...

561
00:56:19.632 --> 00:56:23.472
"Don't waste time waiting
for the perfect man because...

562
00:56:24.184 --> 00:56:27.009
well, life is too goddamned short."

563
00:56:27.954 --> 00:56:30.188
That's what she said?

564
00:56:43.803 --> 00:56:46.801
Wish I could just run away, don't you?

565
00:56:49.174 --> 00:56:51.277
I don't know.

566
00:56:51.377 --> 00:56:55.010
There's nowhere to really run off to.

567
00:56:56.448 --> 00:56:58.852
Where would you even go?

568
00:56:58.952 --> 00:57:01.187
Ever been to the beach?

569
00:57:02.022 --> 00:57:05.362
Never really had a chance to.

570
00:57:05.462 --> 00:57:08.595
That's where I'd go.
Somewhere with a beach.

571
00:57:09.195 --> 00:57:11.080
You could always come
to the beach with me

572
00:57:11.180 --> 00:57:14.885
and, you know, we could have
our sandcastle house.

573
00:57:14.985 --> 00:57:18.222
Go fishing. We'd survive on fish.

574
00:57:19.022 --> 00:57:21.258
Could be a lot worse.

575
00:57:22.242 --> 00:57:26.178
If you could, if there was any place
on Earth you could run away to,

576
00:57:26.278 --> 00:57:28.025
where'd you run?

577
00:57:28.125 --> 00:57:30.334
If I had to choose?

578
00:57:33.319 --> 00:57:35.653
I'd probably go home.

579
00:57:36.722 --> 00:57:38.885
Pretty exciting, right?

580
00:57:38.985 --> 00:57:41.411
Is that in New Mexico?

581
00:57:44.563 --> 00:57:46.530
I don't know.

582
00:58:24.954 --> 00:58:27.001
Well, come on.

583
00:58:27.841 --> 00:58:31.812
- Tell me something about yourself.
- Well, there's not much to tell.

584
00:58:31.912 --> 00:58:36.015
I don't much like talking about myself.
It's not easy for me.

585
00:58:36.115 --> 00:58:38.283
Fine. What about the boy?

586
00:58:39.586 --> 00:58:41.808
His mother died.

587
00:58:45.391 --> 00:58:46.860
And?

588
00:58:46.960 --> 00:58:49.229
I'm taking him to live
with his grandparents.

589
00:58:49.729 --> 00:58:51.664
Well, why go through all that trouble?

590
00:58:52.566 --> 00:58:55.335
Well, because he's a good kid.

591
00:58:55.435 --> 00:58:57.837
I don't mind spending time with him.

592
00:58:59.606 --> 00:59:01.705
What's in it for you?

593
00:59:03.909 --> 00:59:06.277
There ain't nothing in it for me.

594
00:59:08.080 --> 00:59:09.964
You're lying.

595
00:59:10.434 --> 00:59:12.633
You're a liar.

596
00:59:14.820 --> 00:59:16.588
Is he yours?

597
00:59:25.981 --> 00:59:28.048
Look at you.

598
00:59:45.751 --> 00:59:48.221
I ain't no fucking liar.

599
01:00:00.367 --> 01:00:02.736
You're way better.
I'm not even making...

600
01:00:02.836 --> 01:00:04.638
Snap, snap, clap.

601
01:00:04.738 --> 01:00:06.686
I can't snap.

602
01:00:10.402 --> 01:00:13.780
Hey, you know we're not far
from my grandparents' house.

603
01:00:13.880 --> 01:00:17.350
- My mom said it snows there.
- I've never seen snow.

604
01:00:17.450 --> 01:00:20.019
- Really?
- Yeah.

605
01:00:20.419 --> 01:00:24.591
You should come. I mean...
you know, if you wanted.

606
01:00:24.691 --> 01:00:28.389
- It'd be cool.
- Yeah. Sounds fun.

607
01:00:29.579 --> 01:00:31.345
Yeah.

608
01:00:43.409 --> 01:00:47.280
- Yeah?
- <i>Hey, let me talk to George. It's John.</i>

609
01:00:47.380 --> 01:00:49.282
John?

610
01:00:49.382 --> 01:00:52.717
- How's the head?
- Oh, just fine. How's your sister?

611
01:00:59.091 --> 01:01:01.695
Hey, John. Any luck in finding my money?

612
01:01:01.795 --> 01:01:03.697
<i>I've got the rest of your 10,000.</i>

613
01:01:04.197 --> 01:01:06.332
- <i>So you're 10 short.</i>
- How about this?

614
01:01:06.582 --> 01:01:10.336
<i>I bring you what I have.
Or you can come looking for the rest.</i>

615
01:01:10.436 --> 01:01:13.574
Maybe I'll go look for it in New Mexico.

616
01:01:14.474 --> 01:01:16.643
Farmington, New Mexico.

617
01:01:16.743 --> 01:01:19.446
<i>Maybe I'll find my money over there.</i>

618
01:01:19.946 --> 01:01:23.817
- I don't know what you're talking about.
- <i>Of course you don't.</i>

619
01:01:24.987 --> 01:01:26.503
20,000, John.

620
01:01:27.590 --> 01:01:29.687
<i>See you soon.</i>

621
01:01:52.077 --> 01:01:54.564
Our hometown ain't far from here.

622
01:01:54.664 --> 01:01:58.283
- Y'all can stay with us if you want.
- Oh, yeah? How long?

623
01:02:00.019 --> 01:02:01.953
As long as you want.

624
01:02:04.256 --> 01:02:07.227
Yeah, I don't know about that.
I think that...

625
01:02:07.327 --> 01:02:10.564
I think that this little thing
has probably run its course.

626
01:02:10.664 --> 01:02:13.331
So we should probably get going.

627
01:02:19.421 --> 01:02:21.124
Well, fuck you, John.

628
01:02:21.774 --> 01:02:24.951
Well, I think we've already
done that, haven't we?

629
01:02:29.665 --> 01:02:31.251
Louis.

630
01:02:31.351 --> 01:02:33.320
John tell you why he's taking you home?

631
01:02:33.420 --> 01:02:37.224
- Yeah, he's taking me to my grandparents.
- No, baby. Did he tell you why?

632
01:02:37.324 --> 01:02:39.456
I think you should probably quit
while you're ahead.

633
01:02:39.556 --> 01:02:43.400
Well, I think I'd like
to fill in the blanks, okay?

634
01:02:44.064 --> 01:02:46.740
John strikes me
as the type of guy who's failed

635
01:02:46.840 --> 01:02:49.703
at just about everything
he's ever done. Am I right?

636
01:02:49.803 --> 01:02:52.806
You always had luck
with the ladies, didn't you?

637
01:02:53.306 --> 01:02:55.809
But that never lasted.

638
01:02:56.109 --> 01:02:58.111
And somewhere along the way,
all those big plans,

639
01:02:58.211 --> 01:03:01.248
well, they fell apart
and you got desperate.

640
01:03:02.448 --> 01:03:03.917
A little lonely.

641
01:03:04.617 --> 01:03:06.853
That's why the idea
of dragging him around, well...

642
01:03:06.953 --> 01:03:10.323
- wasn't so bad, was it?
- Mom...

643
01:03:10.423 --> 01:03:14.227
Don't worry, honey. He ain't like us.

644
01:03:14.327 --> 01:03:18.598
Men like him don't have the balls
to survive in the real world.

645
01:03:18.698 --> 01:03:19.823
All right, listen, lady...

646
01:03:19.923 --> 01:03:23.470
But the one whose got
the most to lose is you.

647
01:03:23.570 --> 01:03:26.239
Do you even know who he is, honey?

648
01:03:26.639 --> 01:03:28.722
'Cause he's using you.

649
01:03:30.125 --> 01:03:32.509
Just like he used me.

650
01:03:38.050 --> 01:03:40.486
Just like he uses everybody.

651
01:03:40.586 --> 01:03:42.220
This is bullshit.

652
01:03:49.444 --> 01:03:51.346
They always run.

653
01:04:10.382 --> 01:04:13.052
- John? John?
- Get back inside, Louis!

654
01:04:13.152 --> 01:04:14.942
John, let's just leave.

655
01:04:15.042 --> 01:04:19.723
- We can find another ride.
- Louis, get back inside.

656
01:04:24.029 --> 01:04:28.801
- John, she doesn't know anything about you.
- She's right, Louis. I am afraid.

657
01:04:28.901 --> 01:04:31.794
And I just can't take living
like everyone else, you know?

658
01:04:33.106 --> 01:04:35.291
The problem is...

659
01:04:35.391 --> 01:04:38.208
there's certain things about me
that I just can't seem to change.

660
01:04:38.593 --> 01:04:41.637
John. John, stop.

661
01:04:42.431 --> 01:04:44.164
John!

662
01:04:59.598 --> 01:05:03.503
I knew there was something wrong with him.
Come on, Louis. We're gonna take you home.

663
01:05:04.153 --> 01:05:06.720
It's not gonna end well, honey.

664
01:05:08.840 --> 01:05:11.776
Come on, get in. Come on, it's okay.

665
01:05:22.220 --> 01:05:25.196
Louis! What are you doing?

666
01:05:29.621 --> 01:05:31.332
Get over!

667
01:05:32.966 --> 01:05:34.472
Get down!

668
01:05:41.840 --> 01:05:44.076
God damn it!

669
01:05:44.893 --> 01:05:47.263
God damn it!

670
01:05:47.363 --> 01:05:49.916
This is a lot of money.

671
01:05:50.016 --> 01:05:52.507
We could fly to Farmington if we wanted.

672
01:06:05.691 --> 01:06:08.635
You know what she said
about you wasn't true.

673
01:06:09.135 --> 01:06:11.829
I don't know, she split me
wide open, didn't she?

674
01:06:13.573 --> 01:06:15.876
You know, when I was in jail,

675
01:06:15.976 --> 01:06:20.246
everyone wanted to blame everyone else
for who they turned out to be.

676
01:06:20.346 --> 01:06:24.315
Mom, Dad, girlfriend, wife.

677
01:06:26.518 --> 01:06:29.453
I made a lot of mistakes in my life.

678
01:06:31.957 --> 01:06:35.441
But they were my mistakes,
nobody else's.

679
01:06:36.094 --> 01:06:38.131
They're mine.

680
01:06:38.831 --> 01:06:44.095
You know, when you get older, Louis, all
those mistakes start piling up inside you.

681
01:06:45.121 --> 01:06:47.716
Just a pile of mistakes.

682
01:06:49.274 --> 01:06:52.614
Regrets, blame.

683
01:06:55.214 --> 01:06:58.549
It's enough to make you feel
sick to your stomach.

684
01:07:00.852 --> 01:07:03.689
Secrets make me feel like that.

685
01:07:03.789 --> 01:07:06.365
Yeah, secrets, too.

686
01:07:10.328 --> 01:07:13.742
- You got many secrets?
- Yeah, plenty.

687
01:07:14.984 --> 01:07:17.075
How about you?

688
01:07:19.404 --> 01:07:21.274
Yeah.

689
01:07:21.674 --> 01:07:24.208
- I like that girl.
- Shit, that ain't no secret.

690
01:07:28.146 --> 01:07:29.914
Yeah.

691
01:07:34.486 --> 01:07:36.854
Tell me one of your secrets.

692
01:07:41.326 --> 01:07:43.750
Maybe some other time.

693
01:08:33.828 --> 01:08:35.533
John?

694
01:08:46.058 --> 01:08:47.892
John?

695
01:08:53.388 --> 01:08:54.623
John?

696
01:09:09.030 --> 01:09:10.801
Hey!

697
01:09:14.719 --> 01:09:16.753
Look at that.

698
01:09:39.311 --> 01:09:41.814
Hey, we need some food for the road.

699
01:09:41.914 --> 01:09:44.801
All right. I'm gonna go grab some gas.

700
01:09:44.901 --> 01:09:48.535
Let's meet back here in ten minutes.
All right, you go first.

701
01:09:55.143 --> 01:09:57.077
Watch out.

702
01:10:02.083 --> 01:10:03.817
Go on!

703
01:10:10.075 --> 01:10:12.979
<i>Our APO here is 96309.</i>

704
01:10:13.079 --> 01:10:17.049
<i>So drop us a line, anytime,
APO 96309 and we'll get it on.</i>

705
01:10:17.149 --> 01:10:19.786
- Anything else?
- Oh, that's it. Thanks.

706
01:10:19.886 --> 01:10:24.023
<i>This is the 11:00 report featuring
John Marks with the news and sports.</i>

707
01:10:24.123 --> 01:10:26.592
<i>A brazen daytime robbery
of the Alpine Savings Bank</i>

708
01:10:26.692 --> 01:10:29.361
<i>has state police looking
for an unidentified man</i>

709
01:10:29.461 --> 01:10:31.097
<i>and his teenage accomplice.</i>

710
01:10:31.197 --> 01:10:34.367
<i>They were last seen traveling west
on Farm Road 369</i>

711
01:10:34.467 --> 01:10:39.487
<i>in a tan station wagon
with Texas license plates 74EJQ8.</i>

712
01:10:44.910 --> 01:10:48.579
- Are we going to jail?
- Nah, we ain't going to jail.

713
01:10:50.799 --> 01:10:52.834
You scared?

714
01:10:53.452 --> 01:10:54.754
No.

715
01:10:56.921 --> 01:10:58.334
I'm scared.

716
01:10:59.908 --> 01:11:02.158
What are we gonna do?

717
01:11:04.563 --> 01:11:06.596
I don't know.

718
01:11:09.502 --> 01:11:11.927
What a mess.

719
01:11:15.373 --> 01:11:17.741
We should go to Mexico.

720
01:11:18.810 --> 01:11:21.614
We could live there for years
with all this money.

721
01:11:22.181 --> 01:11:24.586
We should get a car, but...

722
01:11:25.785 --> 01:11:27.336
We could do that.

723
01:11:27.436 --> 01:11:29.771
- Give me a rock.
- Oh, I got it.

724
01:12:11.863 --> 01:12:14.000
I liked the station wagon better.

725
01:12:14.550 --> 01:12:16.486
Yeah, well...

726
01:12:16.586 --> 01:12:20.388
nobody's gonna be missing this piece
of shit. I can tell you that much.

727
01:12:21.073 --> 01:12:24.282
Be nice if we could get
this thing up over 50.

728
01:12:24.844 --> 01:12:27.695
I figure we'll drive about halfway there
then find a quiet place

729
01:12:27.795 --> 01:12:29.825
to camp for the night.

730
01:12:30.899 --> 01:12:33.688
- What's it gonna be like?
- What?

731
01:12:34.438 --> 01:12:38.022
- Your grandparents' place?
- Yep.

732
01:12:39.941 --> 01:12:43.577
I don't know.
I imagine it'll be beautiful.

733
01:12:48.466 --> 01:12:50.799
Think we'll be there tomorrow?

734
01:12:51.270 --> 01:12:54.585
Oh, yeah. We should be there by lunch.

735
01:12:56.741 --> 01:12:59.740
First we have to make it
through the desert.

736
01:13:02.013 --> 01:13:04.915
Then we'll cross into the mountains.

737
01:13:07.719 --> 01:13:11.425
We'll know we're getting close
when we can see the farmlands.

738
01:13:12.007 --> 01:13:15.776
Green, as far as the eye can see.

739
01:13:20.998 --> 01:13:23.367
Just like that picture?

740
01:13:25.770 --> 01:13:29.171
Yeah, just like the picture.

741
01:14:38.908 --> 01:14:41.344
Let me get that for you.

742
01:14:46.301 --> 01:14:48.220
There you go.

743
01:14:52.857 --> 01:14:55.261
You're looking good there, partner.

744
01:14:55.361 --> 01:14:57.317
I want to make
a good impression, you know?

745
01:14:57.417 --> 01:14:58.937
Let's go.

746
01:15:23.722 --> 01:15:25.755
Fill it up, will you?

747
01:15:37.936 --> 01:15:40.949
- Morning.
- Good morning.

748
01:16:05.696 --> 01:16:09.783
- He almost finished out there?
- Yeah, almost.

749
01:16:18.009 --> 01:16:20.544
<i>9-1-1. What's your emergency?</i>

750
01:16:21.379 --> 01:16:23.264
<i>Hello?</i>

751
01:16:25.050 --> 01:16:27.617
<i>What's the address of your emergency?</i>

752
01:16:30.639 --> 01:16:35.094
- That'll be it.
- Okay, it's 20 on pump, $24.

753
01:16:35.194 --> 01:16:37.727
24. That's a steal.

754
01:16:43.284 --> 01:16:45.585
You have a good day.

755
01:16:52.393 --> 01:16:53.661
Boy?

756
01:17:01.402 --> 01:17:02.798
You're the one from the paper.

757
01:17:02.898 --> 01:17:07.326
I think you got me confused
with somebody else, all right?

758
01:17:07.426 --> 01:17:10.095
No. I know who you are.

759
01:17:10.195 --> 01:17:12.229
I know who he is too.

760
01:17:28.412 --> 01:17:30.341
The truth...

761
01:17:30.441 --> 01:17:31.971
sir...

762
01:17:37.455 --> 01:17:40.526
The truth is, he's my son...

763
01:17:41.026 --> 01:17:44.118
and all I've ever done
is disappoint him.

764
01:17:47.631 --> 01:17:51.441
I've abandoned him. I've lied to him.

765
01:17:53.071 --> 01:17:55.708
I found every excuse that I can...

766
01:17:55.808 --> 01:17:58.511
just to make him
another mistake in my life.

767
01:17:59.211 --> 01:18:03.196
A secret that I keep to myself.

768
01:18:06.751 --> 01:18:09.052
But he won't let me.

769
01:18:09.621 --> 01:18:13.823
Please, just...
just let me make it right.

770
01:18:15.092 --> 01:18:18.028
Just please let me make it right.

771
01:18:26.204 --> 01:18:28.540
Come on. Grab your bag!

772
01:18:28.640 --> 01:18:30.308
Don't you hear that?

773
01:18:31.543 --> 01:18:33.933
Do you remember the address?

774
01:18:34.780 --> 01:18:35.831
What?

775
01:18:35.931 --> 01:18:39.485
Do you remember what the place looks like?
Do you remember the address?

776
01:18:40.385 --> 01:18:42.489
What's going on?

777
01:18:43.889 --> 01:18:45.877
All right, I need you to leave.

778
01:18:46.258 --> 01:18:47.660
I'm not leaving you.

779
01:18:47.760 --> 01:18:50.562
I promised this guy in there
I wouldn't run

780
01:18:50.662 --> 01:18:53.192
'cause I can't run anymore.

781
01:18:55.417 --> 01:18:58.288
I see myself as the person
that I'm supposed to be.

782
01:18:59.338 --> 01:19:02.408
A good person, the kind of person
that you deserve.

783
01:19:03.198 --> 01:19:05.958
I just... I don't have the courage
to be that person.

784
01:19:06.058 --> 01:19:09.181
I don't have the courage to change.
Do you understand what I'm trying to say?

785
01:19:09.381 --> 01:19:13.089
So here, take this with you.
Take it with you...

786
01:19:14.421 --> 01:19:16.989
and go. I need you to go, all right?
You're gonna be okay.

787
01:19:17.089 --> 01:19:19.528
Hey, you're gonna be all right.

788
01:19:19.628 --> 01:19:20.971
Now go, go, go, go.

789
01:19:21.071 --> 01:19:23.796
I don't want to leave, John.
I don't want to leave you.

790
01:19:23.896 --> 01:19:26.532
You gotta go. You gotta go.

791
01:19:26.632 --> 01:19:31.722
- I don't want to leave you, John.
- Go! Run, god damn it! Run!

792
01:19:46.584 --> 01:19:48.982
Face the car! Hands in the air!

793
01:21:47.922 --> 01:21:50.380
<i>What do you think it's going to be like?</i>

794
01:21:52.644 --> 01:21:55.078
<i>I'd imagine it'd be beautiful.</i>

795
01:21:57.048 --> 01:22:00.616
<i>Surrounded by farmland
as far as the eye can see.</i>

796
01:22:02.404 --> 01:22:04.647
<i>Just like that picture?</i>

797
01:22:06.024 --> 01:22:09.613
<i>Yeah, just like the picture.</i>

798
01:22:38.322 --> 01:22:42.361
<i>We're going to do a quick line inspection
here in Farmington, New Mexico.</i>

799
01:22:42.461 --> 01:22:44.687
<i>Line number seven.</i>

800
01:24:57.861 --> 01:25:00.063
You lost?

801
01:25:07.438 --> 01:25:09.674
I need to get to Farmington.

802
01:25:09.774 --> 01:25:12.078
You are lost.

803
01:25:13.378 --> 01:25:15.213
I'm not lost.

804
01:25:15.695 --> 01:25:17.949
Whatever you say.

805
01:25:18.314 --> 01:25:21.751
Yeah, you're close.

806
01:25:23.321 --> 01:25:27.525
It's up that road about an hour or so.

807
01:25:28.959 --> 01:25:33.479
- An hour?
- Yeah, at least an hour.

808
01:25:34.666 --> 01:25:36.533
But you're young.

809
01:25:43.841 --> 01:25:46.016
You could give me a ride.

810
01:25:47.145 --> 01:25:50.012
I could, yeah.

811
01:25:51.815 --> 01:25:55.482
I'd be a lot more willing
if we was to bargain for it.

812
01:25:56.271 --> 01:26:02.319
Kid with that kind of silver ain't gonna
have a hard time finding a ride home.

813
01:26:05.796 --> 01:26:08.328
How about it, kid?

814
01:26:18.943 --> 01:26:21.453
23 Farm Road.

815
01:26:21.553 --> 01:26:23.627
23 Farm Road.

816
01:27:46.864 --> 01:27:48.454
Louis?

817
01:27:49.534 --> 01:27:53.805
- Hey, Grandma.
- Oh, thank you, Lord!

818
01:27:53.905 --> 01:27:56.686
Oh, we thought we'd lost you forever!

819
01:27:56.786 --> 01:27:58.596
Hi.

820
01:27:59.543 --> 01:28:03.048
You were supposed to be here days ago.

821
01:28:03.498 --> 01:28:07.586
Just look at you. How'd you get here?

822
01:28:08.486 --> 01:28:09.957
I walked.

823
01:28:10.057 --> 01:28:13.059
Oh, Lord.
Well, come on, get in the house.

824
01:28:14.559 --> 01:28:18.061
Where'd you start from?
What do you mean, you walked?

825
01:28:30.107 --> 01:28:33.442
How do you boys get so dirty?

826
01:28:35.013 --> 01:28:37.949
It's good to have you home, sweetheart.

827
01:28:38.349 --> 01:28:41.551
I want this to feel like home, okay?

828
01:28:54.398 --> 01:28:56.892
This was your mother's room.

829
01:29:02.339 --> 01:29:04.274
I kept so many of 'em.

830
01:29:06.259 --> 01:29:08.303
I hope they don't make you sad.

831
01:29:09.647 --> 01:29:11.581
I like looking at 'em.

832
01:29:14.535 --> 01:29:17.503
Makes me feel like she's still here.

833
01:29:19.406 --> 01:29:23.781
You were born in this bed.
This exact one.

834
01:29:24.228 --> 01:29:26.095
Really?

835
01:29:30.134 --> 01:29:31.624
See?

836
01:29:31.724 --> 01:29:35.754
There's your mom
and your dad holding you.

837
01:29:36.974 --> 01:29:39.560
You were just a few months old.

838
01:29:41.295 --> 01:29:45.513
Oh, you've grown so much since then.

839
01:29:47.985 --> 01:29:50.519
Oh, my sweet boy.
